                "All billing is issued in U.S. dollars (USD). Depending on the engagement model, your company receives a consolidated monthly invoice covering the agreed services and selected talent, helping simplify cross-border administration and payment workflows."
            ]
        },
        {
            question: "What should U.S. companies consider when engaging remote talent in Latin America?",
            answers: [
                "The responsibilities depend on the engagement model. With Employer of Record (EOR) or outsourcing structures, the local employing entity manages payroll and employment obligations in the professional's country of residence. Contractor and staff augmentation models require different documentation, classification, and operating arrangements. <br><br> <span style=' font-weight: 900;'>Oberstaff<span style='color: #ff66cc; font-weight: 900;'>.</span></span> helps you understand the available model, expected costs, and operational responsibilities before moving forward. Federal and state tax, employment, and worker-classification obligations can vary by company and engagement structure, so your own legal or tax advisers should confirm any obligations specific to your business."
